WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.506
Performance is trainable capability.

00:00:01.506 --> 00:00:05.374
People improve when they practice the right things, receive useful feedback,

00:00:05.374 --> 00:00:07.131
and correct errors over time.

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:09.241
Experience alone does not guarantee improvement.

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:13.460
Someone can repeat the same pattern for years without getting better if

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.679
the work never exposes weak points or gives them a way to

00:00:17.679 --> 00:00:18.329
adjust.

00:00:18.329 --> 00:00:21.493
Deliberate practice focuses on specific components of a skill.

00:00:21.493 --> 00:00:24.657
Instead of vaguely trying to get better at communication,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.766
a person might practice clearer handoffs.

00:00:26.766 --> 00:00:31.688
Instead of broadly trying to become a better analyst, they might practice evidence evaluation,

00:00:31.688 --> 00:00:33.446
assumption checking, or concise writing.

00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:36.962
Breaking skills into components makes improvement more visible and manageable.

00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:38.368
Feedback loops are essential.

00:00:38.368 --> 00:00:43.290
Good feedback compares intention with outcome and arrives soon enough to influence future behavior.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:47.157
It can come from peers, mentors, metrics, simulation, rehearsal, review sessions,

00:00:47.157 --> 00:00:47.860
or self-reflection.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.025
The goal is not criticism for its own sake.

00:00:51.025 --> 00:00:54.892
The goal is correction that helps future performance become more reliable.

00:00:54.892 --> 00:00:57.001
Challenge should be balanced with recoverability.

00:00:57.001 --> 00:01:00.165
Practice that is too easy does not stretch capability.

00:01:00.165 --> 00:01:03.681
Practice that is too overwhelming can create confusion or discouragement.

00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:07.900
Simulation and rehearsal are useful because they let people prepare for difficult

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.009
work before the stakes are high.

00:01:10.009 --> 00:01:13.877
Improvement is built through repetition with correction, not through busyness alone.

00:01:13.877 --> 00:01:16.689
Deliberate practice also requires selecting the right measure.

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:21.260
Hours spent are easy to count, but they do not always show improvement.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.479
Better measures focus on error rate, clarity, speed with quality, decision accuracy,

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:28.994
handoff quality, or the ability to perform under realistic constraints.

00:01:28.994 --> 00:01:31.860
The measure should reflect the skill that actually matters.
